  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q55-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "55",
    "prompt": "Find the range of $f(x)=\\dfrac{12}{7+3\\cos x-4\\sin x}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$[1,6]$.\n\nThe denominator ranges from $2$ to $12$.",
      "worked": "The amplitude of $3\\cos x-4\\sin x$ is $\\sqrt{3^2+(-4)^2}=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-5&\\le3\\cos x-4\\sin x\\le5\\\\2&\\le7+3\\cos x-4\\sin x\\le12\\\\1&\\le\\frac{12}{7+3\\cos x-4\\sin x}\\le6.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth denominator endpoints are attained, so the range is $[1,6]$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
